[=DESCRIPTION]
\fBfomo\fR is a terminal UI for activating Azure Privileged Identity
Management (PIM) eligible role assignments.
The application queries all eligible role assignments for the signed-in
account and presents them in an interactive, filterable checklist.
Multiple roles can be selected and activated in a single operation;
the activation requests are submitted one after another, and each role's
status is shown as it completes.
.PP
Both Azure RBAC roles (subscription, resource and management-group scope)
and Microsoft Entra ID directory roles are supported.
Management-group activation is only available in the non-interactive
CLI mode (\fB\-\-mg\fR); the TUI has no management-group picker.
.PP
A non-interactive (CLI) mode is available when \fB\-r\fR/\fB\-\-reason\fR is
supplied on the command line together with the role and scope arguments.
This is useful for scripting and automation.
In CLI mode an exact role name (case-insensitive) wins; otherwise every
role whose name contains the given text is activated.
Subscriptions match by name substring or exact ID, and every matching
subscription is used.
Roles that are already active are skipped.
.PP
\fB\-\-demo\fR only affects the TUI.
Combined with \fB\-r\fR/\fB\-\-reason\fR it is currently ignored, so the
command performs a real activation; use \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR to simulate one.
.PP
.B Authentication.
Azure Resource Manager calls go through
.B az rest
and use the active
.BR az (1)
CLI session; \fBfomo\fR never sees those credentials.
Run
.B az login
before using this tool.
.PP
Entra roles are managed through Microsoft Graph, which needs a scope that
the Azure CLI's first-party application does not have.
For these, \fBfomo\fR runs its own OAuth 2.0 device-code sign-in: it shows
a URL and a code, opens a graphical browser when one can be shown (not
over SSH or without a display), and waits for you to sign in.
The resulting access and refresh tokens are handled in-process and the
refresh token is cached in \fI~/.cache/fomo/graph_token.json\fR
(mode 0600), so later runs sign in silently.
The device-code prompt comes back when the cached refresh token expires.
Delete that file to force a fresh sign-in.
.PP
.B Network access.
Besides Azure Resource Manager and Microsoft Graph, \fBfomo\fR downloads
blast-radius tier data from the public
.I emiliensocchi/azure-tiering
GitHub repository and caches it for 7 days in \fI~/.cache/fomo/\fR.

[WORKFLOW]
.TP
.B Step\~1\ \(em\ Select subscriptions
A filterable list of Azure subscriptions is shown on the \fBAzure\fR tab.
Select one or more subscriptions whose eligible roles you want to inspect.
Press \fBEnter\fR to load roles.
.TP
.B Step\~2\ \(em\ Select roles
All eligible PIM roles across the selected subscriptions are merged into a
single filterable list.
Type to narrow the list, use \fBSpace\fR or \fBx\fR to toggle individual
items, then press \fBEnter\fR to proceed.
Selecting more than \fB3\fR roles is allowed but shows a warning, because
large batches can be slow and error-prone.
Roles in a high blast-radius tier (Tier\~0 or Tier\~1) also trigger a warning.
.TP
.B Step\~3\ \(em\ Confirm and activate
Enter a justification (required by Azure PIM), choose an activation duration,
and press \fBEnter\fR or the \fBActivate\fR button.
Each role's activation status is shown in a live table.
Global (management-group-scoped) roles are highlighted separately because
they remain active across all subscriptions under that scope.
.SS Entra tab
The first screen has a second tab, \fBEntra\fR, listing your eligible
Microsoft Entra ID directory roles.
\fBfomo \-\-entra\fR opens the TUI directly on this tab.
The roles are fetched through Microsoft Graph the first time the tab is
shown; this may require the device-code sign-in described under
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR (the URL and code are shown on screen).
Already-active roles are marked.
Select one or more roles and press \fBEnter\fR to continue to the Entra
activation screen.
.SS Entra activation
Like Step\~3: enter a justification, choose a duration and press
\fBActivate\fR.
Each Entra role's status is shown in a live table.
.SS Assignments screen
Press \fBi\fR on the first screen to see your currently active Azure and
Entra role assignments, on separate \fBAzure\fR and \fBEntra\fR tabs.
The Entra tab may require the device-code sign-in.

[KEY BINDINGS]
Key bindings are shown in the footer of each screen and differ slightly
between screens.
Letter keys act on the list; while a filter or text input has focus they
are typed into it instead.
.SS Subscription and Entra tab screen
.TP
.B Enter
On the tab bar, move to the filter.
In the filter, move to the list.
In the list, load roles for the selected subscriptions (Azure tab) or
continue to activation with the selected roles (Entra tab).
.TP
.BR x \ /\  Space
Toggle the highlighted item.
.TP
.B a
Select all listed subscriptions (Azure tab) or all visible roles
(Entra tab).
.TP
.B n
Deselect everything.
.TP
.B /
Move focus to the filter input.
.TP
.B Escape
Toggle focus between the filter input and the list.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-s
Toggle subscription sort (A\(->Z / Z\(->A) on the Azure tab, or cycle the
Entra role sort order (name, tier, expiry) on the Entra tab.
.TP
.BR h \ /\  l
Switch to the previous / next tab.
The \fBLeft\fR and \fBRight\fR arrow keys do the same while the tab bar has
focus.
.TP
.B i
Open the assignments screen.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SS Role selection screen
.TP
.B Enter
Proceed to the activation screen with the selected roles.
In the filter, move to the list instead.
.TP
.BR x \ /\  Space
Toggle the highlighted role.
.TP
.B a
Select all visible (filtered) roles.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-s
Cycle the sort order (name, scope, tier, expiry).
Defaults to alphabetical.
.TP
.B Tab
Move focus from the filter to the list.
.TP
.B Shift\-Tab
Move focus from the list to the filter.
.TP
.B /
Move focus to the filter input.
.TP
.BR Escape \ /\  q
Return to the subscription screen.
.SS Activation screens (Azure and Entra)
.TP
.B Enter
In the reason (justification) field, activate the roles.
With an empty reason, show a warning instead.
.TP
.B Tab
Move from the reason field to the duration selector.
.TP
.B Escape
Return to the role selection screen.
On the Azure activation screen, the first \fBEscape\fR only leaves the
justification field.
Going back is not possible while an activation is running.
.TP
.B q
Return to the previous screen (Entra activation screen only).
.SS Assignments screen
.TP
.BR 1 \ /\  2 \ /\  3 \ /\  4
Sort the focused table by role, scope, expiry or type.
Pressing the same key again reverses the order.
.TP
.B r
Reload both tabs, for example after \fBaz login\fR or after deleting
\fI~/.cache/fomo/graph_token.json\fR to sign in to Graph again.
.TP
.BR Escape \ /\  q
Return to the subscription screen.
.SS Navigation (list screens)
.TP
.BR j \ /\  k
Move down / up (Vim-style).
.TP
.BR g \ /\  G
Jump to first / last item.

[EXAMPLES]
Launch the interactive TUI:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fomo
.EE
.RE
.PP
Open the TUI on the Entra tab:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fomo \-\-entra
.EE
.RE
.PP
Simulate the full activation flow without making any write calls
(roles are still read from Azure):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fomo \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Explore the TUI with built-in demo data, no Azure account needed:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fomo \-\-demo
.EE
.RE
.PP
Capture verbose debug output to a file for troubleshooting:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fomo \-\-log /tmp/fomo.log
.EE
.RE
.PP
Then inspect the log:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
grep 'az rest' /tmp/fomo.log
.EE
.RE
.PP
.B Non-interactive (CLI) mode
.PP
Activate an Azure RBAC role on a subscription without the TUI
(SUBSCRIPTION and ROLE names accept substrings):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fomo my-sub "Key Vault Administrator" \-r "Break-glass access" \-t 1h
.EE
.RE
.PP
Activate a role scoped to a management group:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fomo \-\-mg my-mg "Reader" \-r "Audit review" \-t 30m
.EE
.RE
.PP
Activate a Microsoft Entra ID role:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fomo \-\-entra "Global Reader" \-r "Audit review" \-t 1h
.EE
.RE
.PP
Dry-run a CLI activation (no write calls):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fomo my-sub "Contributor" \-r "Test" \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.RE

[FILES]
.TP
.I ~/.cache/fomo/graph_token.json
Cached Microsoft Graph refresh token for Entra role management (mode 0600).
Delete it to force a new device-code sign-in.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/fomo/tiering_azure.json\fR,\fI ~/.cache/fomo/tiering_entra.json
Blast-radius tier data downloaded from the
.I emiliensocchi/azure-tiering
GitHub repository.
Refreshed when older than 7 days.

[ENVIRONMENT]
.TP
.B PATH
\fBfomo\fR makes all Azure Resource Manager calls through the
.BR az (1)
CLI.
The
.B az
executable must be on
.B PATH
and the session must be authenticated (\fBaz login\fR).
.TP
.B HOME
The token and tiering caches live in \fI$HOME/.cache/fomo/\fR
(see \fBFILES\fR).
.TP
.B TERM
A terminal emulator that supports 256 colours and Unicode is recommended
for the best rendering of the Textual TUI.

[SEE ALSO]
.BR az (1),
.BR az\-login (1)
.PP
